abstract: >-
  NV-diamond spectrum simulation, scalar and vector field estimation, and
  bounded neural correction to PID on a PolarFire SoC development kit.
  A kit-resident processor-paced loop completed an 8.01-hour soak at 3,319 Hz
  with replayed input. On 512 held-out synthetic spectra, kit INT8 outputs
  matched CPU INT8 outputs bit for bit. Jason directed coding agents across
  the build and checked written claims with local language-model critics.
  The repository links each measurement to its report and conditions.
